// A cart presses a tread plate under its rails: a treadle in the track bed. A plate is built into the bed under the
// end of a track, a pull-rod running on from it; a cart let go on the slope above rolls down and stops at the end, over
// the plate, and its weight comes through the rails onto it: the rod is pulled.
map
############################################################
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#..........................................................#
#.@........................................................#
#######====................................................#
#......####====............................................#
#......########====........................................#
#......############====....................................#
#......################==============......................#
#......##########################eeeeFFFFFF................#
#......#####################################################
############################################################
end
give Cart 1
place 2 7 1 Cart
expect 3 carts == 1
expect 30 pulled:32,6 == 0           // the cart is still up the slope
expect 400 cartx > 33                // at the end of the track...
expect 400 pulled:32,6 == 1          // ...over the plate: the rod is pulled
